<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Fascist Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a>–<a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Partito Nazionale Fascista, PNF</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Fascist Party was the far-right party founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in November 1921 as the political expression of Italian fascism, reorganising the earlier Italian Fasces of Combat. It ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/march-on-rome">March on Rome</a> in 1922, and from 1925 it was effectively the only legal party, a status formalised by a law of 1928. Its Blackshirt squads violently suppressed socialist organisations, and the Socialist leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giacomo-matteotti">Giacomo Matteotti</a> was kidnapped and killed by fascist blackshirts. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-of-fascism">Grand Council of Fascism</a> deposed Mussolini on 25 July 1943 the party was banned, and the Constitution of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> forbids its re-formation.</p></div>
